5.10  2026-09-27

  - Fixed a `dashboard serve --foreground` startup hang for any skill
    declaring a collector: CollectorRunner::_find_running_loop scanned
    every /proc PID and fell back to spawning a `ps -o args= -p $pid`
    subprocess whenever a candidate's cmdline was readable-but-empty -
    the permanent, non-racy shape of a kernel thread, not just a
    vanished-process race. On a host with hundreds of kernel threads that
    cost one subprocess spawn per thread, sequentially, making the
    startup hang 90+ seconds with zero output. Now skips a
    readable-but-empty cmdline candidate before ever calling
    _read_process_title, since it can never match a collector's own
    non-empty process title.

5.09  2026-09-27

  - Fixed a dependency-scan masking defect: _locate_module_runtime_file
    walked @INC/roots and returned the FIRST existing file for a module
    name, discarding the dependency scan's own already-known source_path
    for that module. If an earlier @INC entry held a stale/duplicate copy
    of the module, the wrong file was silently bundled into a compiled
    standalone binary. _locate_module_runtime_file now accepts an optional
    known_source_paths lookup (built in _runtime_selected_files from
    %args{dependencies}) and prefers it over the @INC walk.

5.08  2026-09-27

  - Fixed a compiled-standalone-binary crash: three closures in
    StandaloneRuntime.pm's recursive merge/collect ops
    (config_merge_hashes, skill_dispatcher_merge_skill_hashes,
    suggest_collect_skill_commands) resolved their own recursion via
    _code_for($name), the bare unqualified sub name, instead of
    _code_for($full), the package-qualified name available in the same
    scope - _code_for() does a raw typeglob lookup, so the bare name
    resolved against the wrong package and returned undef, crashing
    `dashboard init`.

