4.78  2026-09-22

  - DD-1020: `_compile_launcher`'s objcopy invocations previously hardcoded
    an x86_64 `--output`/`--binary-architecture` spec unconditionally,
    breaking non-x86_64 PAX build hosts - confirmed live in real CI, where
    linux-arm64 and linux-i686 both failed at the objcopy step while
    linux-amd64 succeeded fully. Added `_objcopy_target_for_arch`, which
    detects the build host's real architecture from `$Config{archname}`
    and selects the correct objcopy target pair, verified against the
    real objcopy/binutils tool for x86_64/i686/aarch64. Unblocks DDE-006's
    linux-i686 and linux-arm64 multi-platform PAX CI targets.

