    reference the real, current,
    shipping identifier __PAX_RUNTIME_LEGACY_NAMESPACE__ and describe it in
    prose as a "legacy-namespace alias" - the DD-931 entry uses that phrase
    without the literal identifier present on the same line, so an
    identifier-only exemption did not close the gate (owner decision,
    Q-179). Widened the allow-list (a new _strip_legacy_namespace_mentions
    helper in t/15-release-metadata.t) to also strip the phrase
    "legacy-namespace" case-insensitively before the check runs, alongside
    the existing identifier exemption, while a genuinely retired bare
    mention of that same banned term anywhere else still fails the gate.
    No FIXED_BUGS.md entry was reworded.

4.64  2026-09-21

  - DD-926: pax build's intermediate build cache directory
    (.pax-launcher-build, under Developer::Dashboard::Pax::StandaloneImage's
    _compile_launcher) was a single literal path shared by every uid that
    ever built against the same output parent directory (commonly bare
    /tmp). A root-owned build (e.g. from inside a developer-dashboard:latest
    container) left it root-owned, permanently breaking every later
    non-root build sharing that output parent with a Permission Denied that
    did not self-clear. Namespaced the directory per invoking uid
    (.pax-launcher-build-<uid>, via a new _pax_launcher_build_dir_name
    helper), the same technique File::Temp uses to avoid this exact
    shared-/tmp collision class. Cache reuse within one uid's repeated
    builds is unchanged.

