4.61  2026-09-21

  - DD-985: fixed a path-traversal vulnerability (CWE-22) in
    'dashboard of'/open-file's exact-match fast path
    (_scope_relative_path_match). A '..' segment in the search
    pattern escaped the resolved scope directory entirely, so
    ordinary usage such as 'dashboard of myproject ../../.ssh
    id_rsa' could open or print any file readable by the invoking
    user, with no special flag required. Fixed by resolving through
    the project's existing lexical containment helper
    (_contained_cache_path, the same one DD-498's Zip Slip fix
    established) instead of a second bespoke check. The
    regex-search fallback path was confirmed structurally
    non-vulnerable and left untouched.

4.60  2026-09-21

  - DD-979: new .env/.env.pl skill include feature. A "# include
    <foo.bar>" comment directive in a plain .env file (or "# include
    <foo.bar.*>" to also pull in every nested sub-skill) loads that
    skill's own .env/.env.pl into the current environment on request;
    env->include('foo.bar') does the same programmatically from a
    .env.pl file after `use Developer::Dashboard;`. env is a real
    second package (Perl resolves a bareword before -> as a literal
    package name at parse time, so it cannot be a plain exported sub
    like d2). Included variables are namespaced
    <UPPERCASE.DOTTED.PATH with single underscores>__<name> (foo.bar's
    BOB=1 becomes FOO_BAR__BOB), resolved DD-OOP-LAYERS-style across
    every layer with deeper layers winning without dropping
    shallower-only keys. Hardened against a path-traversal exposure
    found during implementation (a spec like "../.." surviving the
    dot-split as a bare "/" segment) with an explicit _valid_segment()
    guard. New module Developer::Dashboard::EnvInclude, 100.0/100.0/
    100.0/100.0 coverage, 42 new tests, new SYSTEM-scoped doc
    docs/env-skill-include-directive.md.

